  "id": "DrugBank_DB00488 - MONDO_18171",
  "verbalization": "Altretamine is shown to have a clinically relevant indication for Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, as well as for Malignant Dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, through multiple indirect pathways. These pathways suggest a potential role for Altretamine in the treatment of germ cell tumors, as it is linked to a disease entity that is classified under the broader category of \"Malignant Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary.\" The presence of a direct indication for Altretamine in this disease, along with the indirect pathways involving Tretamine and Belotecan, indicates a possible mechanistic link that could be explored further. The evidence suggests that Altretamine may act through a mechanism that influences germ cell tumor biology, though the exact mode of action remains to be determined. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Altretamine could be a candidate for repurposing in the treatment of malignant germ cell tumors of the ovary, provided additional experimental validation is conducted.",
